Title: AROS: refuse file names the system character set cannot hold
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: When a UTF-8 name could not be converted to the system character set, to_system_path (0025) passed the UTF-8 bytes to the file system; a file could be created under a wrong name instead of the operation failing.
Change: to_system_path(utf8, out) returns false for such a name; to_system_path(utf8) throws std::runtime_error with the name and the character set. Queries (is_file, is_directory, file_size, stat-based checks, realpath, opendir/list_files, the file tree, the program icon) treat the name as absent; open_file returns nullptr with errno EILSEQ, and open_file_with_exception says the name uses characters this system cannot store; mkdir, rename, copy, unlink, chmod, rmdir and FSTREAM_PATH throw.
Scope: AROS
Upstream: local-only
Verification: ABIv11 (AROS One, pool v11-3, 2026-11-16), no CHARSET set: "test-ж.png" pasted from the clipboard into Save As (SYS:) gives "Cannot open SYS:test-ж.png: the name uses characters this system cannot store"; List SYS:test#? finds nothing after the run. Polish names on v1 (0025 tests) unaffected in code path.
Removal: AROS-specific.
---
